{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["And the sense of <b>and they shall judge the people at all times</b> is that when there are many judges available, the oppressed person can go to a judge at whatever time he wishes and find him ready, for to you [Moses] he cannot approach at every moment because of the great throng before you and the heavy preoccupation upon you. And many of them will endure the wrong done to them because the opportunity will not arise for them to tell it to you, and they will not want to leave their work and their affairs until the leisure hour arrives when they could approach you.\n<br>And this is the sense of <b>he shall come to his place in peace</b> — for now, since they cannot come to judgment at all times, they will not rest in peace, for this is an opening for robbers to do violence and for oppressors to cause strife. And the sense of <b>to his place</b> is: to whatever place they may come, while they are in the camp in the wilderness. And our Sages (Sanhedrin 34b) drew an inference from the expression <b>and they shall judge the people at all times</b>, that monetary cases may be concluded even at night, for it does not say \"all the day\":"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:11:12.159387370Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}